  "configuration": {
    "name": "Georgia Mountain Fairgrounds",
    "welcome": "Camp beside Lake Chatuge in Hiawassee, Georgia. Area I supports tents and RVs seasonally, April through October; Area II has paved RV sites and operates year-round. Facilities include water, 20/30/50-amp service, Wi-Fi subject to availability, a boat ramp, playground, recreation courts, picnic tables, gardens and on-site security. Area I has no sewer hookups; Area II lists 118 sewer connections, with B1 excluded. Contact the office to confirm site suitability and current availability.",
    "address": "1311 Music Hall Road, Hiawassee, GA 30546\nMail: PO Box 444, Hiawassee, GA 30546",
    "contact_phone": "(706) 896-4191",
    "website_url": "https://georgiamountainfairgrounds.com/pageserver/campgrounds",
    "map_url": "https://georgiamountainfairgrounds.com/pageserver/campground-map",
    "rate_information": "Published reference rates in USD; confirm with the office before reserving. Daily / weekly / monthly:\nArea I tents: $35 / $225 / $575\nArea I lakeside RV: $50 / $300 / $775\nArea I inland RV: $45 / $250 / $675\nArea II B1 (no sewer): $50 / $325 / $775\nArea II lakeside RV: $60 / $400 / $1,000\nArea II inland RV: $55 / $350 / $875\nThe linked 2026 PDF instead lists $975 monthly for Area II lakeside RV sites; this remains unresolved.\nOverflow without hookups: $25 daily, only when the campground is full and the office permits it. Non-camper trailer parking: $5 daily, up to two weeks. These reference rates are not automated quotes or payment collection.",
    "rules": "Keep pets leashed, clean up after them, and limit them to two per site; pet pens are prohibited. Supervise children. Observe quiet hours, 10 p.m.\u20137 a.m. Firearms and fireworks are prohibited; alcohol is prohibited in public-use areas. Use fire rings only. Protect plants and wildlife. Bag rubbish for dumpsters and leave sites clean. Do not wash vehicles or dishes at shared drinking-water or comfort facilities. Dispose of wastewater at designated dump stations. Unauthorized structures and docks are prohibited. Golf carts are restricted to the stated accessibility exception. Register vehicles and display office-issued tags; keep roads and neighboring sites clear. Extra vehicles need office registration. Tents are restricted to Area I. Use designated sites and follow office instructions for overflow. Do not sublet, occupy someone else\u2019s site, or cut through neighboring sites. Register boats with the office and observe mooring restrictions. Campers are responsible for damage and must cooperate with security. Consult the official rules for full terms. For emergencies call 911; contact the campground office for routine assistance.",
    "reservation_policy": "Minimum stay: two nights. Check-in is 3 p.m.; checkout is 1 p.m. Late departures require office arrangements and may incur another day\u2019s charge. The office publishes a 50% deposit due within seven days; unpaid reservations may be released. Refund requests require at least 48 hours\u2019 notice. Cancellation charges are one daily rental, $75 weekly, or $150 monthly. Monthly reservations open on the first working day of November for the following year; shorter stays open on the first working day of January. Opening-day reservations are by phone, one site per call, without phone passing. Site assignments may change. Contact the office for monthly stays, deposits, refunds, seasonal restrictions and final terms. This application does not collect card data or process payments.\nOnline booking is not yet open here. Imported map entries are inactive drafts pending verification of identifiers, capacities, hookups, seasonal dates and map positions. The website reports 207 total sites but its area figures total 212; the older map also needs reconciliation.",
    "policy_version": "gmf-reference-2026-11-24",
    "min_nights": 2
  },
